## What this derivative changes

Upstream is a 5-port USB-C Power Delivery distribution board fed from a 300W
24V supply. It performs **no power conversion** -- it is a passive fan-out
carrying one master switch, fusing, TVS clamping, bulk capacitance, and headers
for five purchased PD modules and one purchased buck module.

This derivative inverts that: **conversion is the board.** The reason is that
the target load is incompatible with upstream's output. A Minisforum MS-01
takes 19V through a barrel jack and cannot be powered over USB-C, so every
USB-C PD module, the PD-specific board and the 24V rail are discarded.

### Retained from upstream

| Element | How it is used |
|---|---|
| 19" chassis geometry (`.stp` B-rep solids) | Dimensional reference, `reference/upstream-19in/` |
| Per-channel fuse + TVS + bulk capacitor pattern | Inherited, rescaled (3A -> 5A; TVS standoff 26V -> 58V bus / 24V output) |
| Master switch via front-panel latching button | Concept inherited; implementation changed -- see below |
| Fan rail derived from the switched main rail | Inherited, with MCU PWM control added |
| CERN-OHL-S v2 licensing | Required, not optional |

### Replaced or discarded

| Element | Disposition |
|---|---|
| 24V rail, HRP-300-24 supply | Replaced by a 48V rail, Mean Well RSP-750-48 |
| 5x XPM52C USB-C PD modules | Discarded -- the load cannot use them |
| Passive fan-out power path | Replaced by 6x LM5116 synchronous buck channels, 48V -> 19V @ 7A |
| Master high-side P-FET (15A commutation) | Replaced by the PSU's built-in remote ON/OFF (CN50 pin 13/14) |
| 2-layer / 2oz / 15A stackup | Replaced by 4-layer, 2oz outer / 1oz inner |
| 10" chassis variants | Removed -- out of scope |
| Upstream gerbers, ODB++, BOM, schematic PDFs | Removed from the working tree. They remain available upstream and in this repository's git history; `docs/upstream-analysis.md` records what was extracted from them |

### Added

- Per-channel synchronous buck conversion (48V -> 19V, 7A)
- Per-channel MCU-independent overvoltage protection with an SCR crowbar
- Per-channel INA226 voltage / current / power telemetry
- ESP32-S3 control board with wired Ethernet, Prometheus metrics and OTA
- Front-panel colour touchscreen running as a separate, non-authoritative device
- Parametric FreeCAD mechanical source

## On editable source

CERN-OHL-S v2 requires the **Source** -- the preferred form for making
modifications. Upstream's current tree holds only exports (STEP/STL,
Gerbers, ODB++, PDFs), but its KiCad project and SolidWorks parts were
committed in December 2025 and removed from the tree in February 2026 (commit
724920b). They remain in the git history this fork carries. An earlier version
of this notice said the originals were withheld; that was wrong, and was
corrected on 2026-09-30.

Exports are not Source. This derivative publishes the KiCad projects and the
parametric FreeCAD scripts, and treats the generated STEP/STL/Gerber files as
what they are -- outputs.

## Defect found in upstream

Upstream's `Q1` is listed as `NCEP40PT15D` (N-channel, 40V) in the README BOM
but as `IRF9540NPBF` (P-channel, 100V) in the JLCPCB `bom.csv`. These are
opposite polarity and not interchangeable. The surrounding gate network --
100k pull-up, 12V zener clamp, pulled low to turn on -- is unambiguously a
P-channel high-side switch, so the CSV is correct and the README is wrong.
Building from the README alone yields a non-functioning board.

Reported here for the benefit of anyone else working from that repository.
The affected circuit is not inherited by this derivative.
